cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use sosfuse2 or the data it ships, please cite it as below. The project's own tables are CC0 1.0;
  tables derived from third-party data (CIE, TSIS-1 HSRS, IUP Bremen, LOWTRAN7) keep their publishers' terms and
  citations, listed in THIRD_PARTY.md and src/sosfuse2/assets/README.md.
title: "sosfuse2: successive-orders-of-scattering twilight sky radiance tables"
type: software
version: 1.5.1
date-released: 2026-11-15
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: sosfuse2 developers
abstract: >-
  Polarized successive-orders-of-scattering solver for the twilight sky in a spherical-shell atmosphere with a
  tropospheric aerosol layer, a stratospheric sulfate layer and absorption by ozone, NO₂ and O₄. NumPy reference implementation,
  optional CUDA kernel through CuPy/NVRTC, tolerance-based numeric gates and signed provenance records for the baked tables.
keywords:
  - twilight
  - sky radiance
  - radiative transfer
  - successive orders of scattering
  - polarization
  - stratospheric aerosol
